# Build output (any directory: platform/simulator/{bin,obj}, ./build, ...)
obj/
bin/
build/
# A cross build needs its own directory, because the toolchain is fixed when that
# directory is created and cannot be swapped afterwards - so avr-dx and the simulator
# cannot share one.
build-*/

# CMake
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake
compile_commands.json

# PlatformIO (ESP32 backend)
.pio/

# Network credentials of the ESP32 backend (local only, see WordclockConfiguration.h)
WordclockSecrets.h

# Settings the simulator persists next to wherever it was started
wordclock-settings.bin

# Dev container feature lock files (auto-generated)
devcontainer-lock.json

# Site-specific dev container variant (local only)
/.devcontainer/vector/

# Working copies an agent checks out beside the repository. They are git worktrees, so
# git offers to record them as a gitlink - which would commit a pointer to a checkout that
# exists on one machine.
/.claude/worktrees/

# Personal Claude Code permission grants. Only the .local. tier: a committed
# .claude/settings.json holds project conventions and stays tracked, whereas these
# grants authorize pushing and closing pull requests as whoever is logged in here,
# which is not something a fresh clone should inherit without deciding it.
/.claude/settings.local.json

# The embed script is imported directly when its comment stripping is being checked, and
# CPython leaves this behind whenever that happens.
__pycache__/
# The tool environment: CI's uv sync makes it here, and in the dev container it is a link to the
# image's /opt/wordclock-env. No trailing slash, which would match the directory and not the link.
.venv

# Logs a run leaves in the working tree - the screenshot recipe in CLAUDE.md writes run.log, and
# a clang-tidy log was once committed by accident.
*.log

# CLion writes a whole project directory here, and all of it but one file is derivable from
# CMakeLists.txt and rewritten whenever the IDE feels like it. The exception is editor.xml,
# which is where the three inspections this project switches off are actually switched off
# - docs/code-inspections.md says which three and why, and would otherwise name a file that
# is not there. So the directory is ignored and that one file is excepted back in.
/.idea/*
!/.idea/editor.xml

# The web pages linters, installed by `make web-lint` from package-lock.json
node_modules/
